{%- comment -%}
  How many pieces are in the collection the row is showing.

  The source order keeps the block portable without asking for duplicate work:
  an explicitly chosen collection wins, then the nearest collection context,
  then `section.settings.collection` for the products row it originally
  described.

  **The count is the collection's, not the row's.** A row showing eight of
  twenty-four pieces says twenty-four, because that is what the number is for —
  it tells a shopper how much more there is, which is also why it reads well
  beside "View All". `all_products_count` is the whole collection whatever the
  row's own limit.

  **The sentence is Liquid's.** Pluralisation belongs in the locale file, as it
  does for the bag count and the card's Add to Bag labels, so nothing here
  assembles a number and a word in the browser or in the schema.

  Renders nothing at all when none of those sources supplies a collection —
  there is no honest number to print, and an empty label would leave a gap in
  the row.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign row_collection = closest.collection
  if block.settings.collection != blank
    assign row_collection = block.settings.collection
  endif
  if row_collection == blank
    assign row_collection = collections[section.settings.collection]
  endif
-%}

{%- if row_collection != blank -%}
  <span class="micro products-list__count reveal" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    {{- 'collections.product_count' | t: count: row_collection.all_products_count -}}
  </span>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.product_count.name",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:blocks.all.content_source_header"
    },
    {
      "type": "collection",
      "id": "collection",
      "label": "t:blocks.all.collection_source.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.product_count.info"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:blocks.product_count.name",
      "settings": {
        "collection": "{{ closest.collection }}"
      }
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
